        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent inpatient stay of your patient, a 67-year-old female, admitted on 23/03/2005 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Diagnostic workup included arterial blood gas analysis confirming hypoxaemic respiratory failure, chest X-ray showing hyperinflation without consolidation, and blood tests revealing mild inflammatory markers. ECG showed no acute cardiac pathology. She was treated with supplemental oxygen therapy, nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, and intravenous fluids. Clinical monitoring included repeated pulse oximetry and vital signs assessment. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. She was discharged home on 24/03/2005 with inhaled bronchodilators and a short oral steroid course. Follow-up in your practice and pulmonary rehabilitation are recommended. Please do not hesitate to contact me with any questions.</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "8648-8",
